Relevant columns and their potential usage
• "project_short_name": limits the analysis to the TCGA‑BRCA project  
• "sample_type_name": picks only the “Solid Tissue Normal” samples  
• "gene_type": keeps only “protein_coding” genes  
• "HTSeq__FPKM_UQ": the numeric expression value whose variance we want  
• "gene_name": human‑readable gene symbol for grouping / reporting  
• "Ensembl_gene_id": unique gene identifier for grouping / reporting  
• "case_barcode": identifies a TCGA case; used to make sure we only work with BRCA cases that actually have ≥1 Solid‑Tissue‑Normal sample  

Possible conditions that may be used
1. "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'  
2. "sample_type_name" = 'Solid Tissue Normal'  
3. "gene_type" = 'protein_coding'  
4. Only include "case_barcode" values that possess at least one row where the sample_type_name is ‘Solid Tissue Normal’.  
   (This can be expressed with a sub‑query or QUALIFY + COUNT … OVER.)  

Below are ten example Snowflake SQL queries, ordered from quick exploratory queries to a full aggregation that could provide the final answer.  Every column name is enclosed in double quotes, all queries use the only table supplied: TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28.  Each query is capped with LIMIT 20 so you can peek at the resulting rows.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at the distinct sample types present in the BRCA project.
SELECT DISTINCT "sample_type_name"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Check the distinct gene types for BRCA records.
SELECT DISTINCT "gene_type"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: List a few BRCA solid‑tissue‑normal rows just to eyeball the data.
SELECT "case_barcode",
       "sample_barcode",
       "gene_name",
       "gene_type",
       "HTSeq__FPKM_UQ"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_type_name" = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Distinct BRCA case barcodes that have at least one Solid Tissue Normal sample.
SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_type_name" = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Count how many protein‑coding genes appear per Solid Tissue Normal sample.
SELECT "sample_barcode",
       COUNT(*) AS "num_protein_coding_genes"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_type_name" = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
  AND "gene_type" = 'protein_coding'
GROUP BY "sample_barcode"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Pull raw FPKM_UQ values for one illustrative gene across Solid Tissue Normal BRCA samples.
SELECT "gene_name",
       "sample_barcode",
       "HTSeq__FPKM_UQ"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_type_name" = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
  AND "gene_type" = 'protein_coding'
  AND "gene_name" = 'TP53'          -- example gene, change as desired
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Compute the variance of FPKM_UQ for every protein‑coding gene in BRCA Solid Tissue Normal samples.
SELECT "gene_name",
       "Ensembl_gene_id",
       VAR_SAMP("HTSeq__FPKM_UQ")  AS "var_fpkm_uq"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_type_name" = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
  AND "gene_type" = 'protein_coding'
GROUP BY "gene_name", "Ensembl_gene_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Rank genes by variance (highest first), still looking only at Solid Tissue Normal BRCA rows.
SELECT "gene_name",
       "Ensembl_gene_id",
       VAR_SAMP("HTSeq__FPKM_UQ") AS "var_fpkm_uq"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name"   = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_type_name"     = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
  AND "gene_type"            = 'protein_coding'
GROUP BY "gene_name", "Ensembl_gene_id"
ORDER BY "var_fpkm_uq" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Restrict to BRCA cases that actually have at least one Solid Tissue Normal sample,
--     then compute gene‑level FPKM_UQ variance for those cases only.
WITH brca_cases_with_normals AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode"
    FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
    WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
      AND "sample_type_name"   = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
)
SELECT r."gene_name",
       r."Ensembl_gene_id",
       VAR_SAMP(r."HTSeq__FPKM_UQ") AS "var_fpkm_uq"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28 r
JOIN brca_cases_with_normals c
  ON r."case_barcode" = c."case_barcode"
WHERE r."sample_type_name" = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
  AND r."gene_type"        = 'protein_coding'
GROUP BY r."gene_name", r."Ensembl_gene_id"
ORDER BY "var_fpkm_uq" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final step — pull the top five protein‑coding genes
--      with the highest FPKM_UQ variance in BRCA Solid Tissue Normal samples.
WITH brca_cases_with_normals AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode"
    FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
    WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
      AND "sample_type_name"   = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
)
SELECT r."gene_name",
       r."Ensembl_gene_id",
       VAR_SAMP(r."HTSeq__FPKM_UQ") AS "var_fpkm_uq"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28 r
JOIN brca_cases_with_normals c
  ON r."case_barcode" = c."case_barcode"
WHERE r."sample_type_name" = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
  AND r."gene_type"        = 'protein_coding'
GROUP BY r."gene_name", r."Ensembl_gene_id"
ORDER BY "var_fpkm_uq" DESC
LIMIT 5;
```

